# Explain logic ASCII (cursor-packs)

**CONSTRAINT:** When this turn explains how existing logic runs (step order,
what runs in parallel, what waits, what a shared timer or deadline does, or
prefetch vs durable write), MUST Read and follow skill `explain-logic-ascii`
before the final user-facing reply.

- MUST: Name the pieces in prose, then include a fenced `text` ASCII TIME
  diagram per the skill.
- MUST NOT: Dump the full skill body into the reply.
- MUST NOT: Use Mermaid as the only figure when order, fan-out, or a shared
  deadline is the point.
- MUST NOT: Replace skill `explain-implementation` channel headings on an
  implement/fix turn; MAY add an ASCII TIME block inside `Explanation` when
  control flow matters.
- MUST NOT: Fire on a yes/no with no mechanism, or when the user only asked for
  a symbol lookup with no control-flow story.

Enforcement: If the reply describes pipelines, phases, or sequential vs
parallel behavior, confirm the skill was read and a TIME diagram is present.
Violation: STOP, Read the skill, add the diagram, then send.

CORRECT:

```text
Prefetch chats many items in parallel; classify writes one row at a time.
Both share one job timer.

[ASCII TIME diagram with Goal lines and timer-death branch]
```

PROHIBITED:

```text
Yes, essence is parallel. [Mermaid-only flowchart, no TIME axis or Goal lines]
```

Chat voice remains rule `always-rules-01-human-interaction`. This rule adds the
ASCII TIME figure when explaining control flow.
